.TH start-tunnel-port-forward-set-enabled 1  "set-enabled "
.SH NAME
start\-tunnel\-port\-forward\-set\-enabled \- Enable or disable a port forward
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBstart\-tunnel port\-forward set\-enabled\fR [\fB\-\-protocol\fR] [\fB\-\-enabled\fR] [\fB\-\-hostname\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISOURCE\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Enable or disable a port forward
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-protocol\fR \fI<PROTOCOL>\fR [default: tcp]
Transport for hostname routes and fallbacks; plain DNAT forwards use both transports
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
tcp
.IP \(bu 2
udp
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-enabled\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-hostname\fR \fI<HOSTNAME>\fR
Selects a hostname; omitted toggles this transport’s fallback or a plain forward
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISOURCE\fR>

